        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Duel">Duel</ref> 9.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Duel 9.1" corresp="#wit-lat"><pb n="431" ed="#liebermann"/>Uersus. Apprehende arma et scutum et exsurge in adiutorium ei, ne gaudeat.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann"/>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">34, 2</note>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 431 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude-crib" ana="#fromLatin" corresp="#wit-lat">Verse. Take hold of arms and shield and rise up to help him. Lest … rejoice.</ab>
      </div>
